{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For you I have seen righteous before Me in this generation.</b> Why did He not say this to him immediately when He commanded him concerning the building of the ark? Because the matter was still in doubt — perhaps they would repent. And furthermore, Methuselah was still alive, so how could He say, 'For you I have seen righteous'? But after HaShem waited the seven days of mourning for Methuselah, as it says (Genesis 7:4), ״כִּי לְיָמִים עוֹד שִׁבְעָה״ — what is the force of 'עוֹד'? Rather, it teaches that this period is equivalent to the period of one hundred and twenty years: for just as He waited one hundred and twenty years for them, perhaps they would repent, so too He waited these seven days of mourning, perhaps they would repent, for through mourning and eulogy the living takes it to heart (Ecclesiastes 7:2). And after they stood firm in their rebellion, He said, 'For you I have seen righteous before Me.' And as for why it does not say 'righteous and wholehearted' — for it says (Genesis 6:9), ״תָּמִים הָיָה בְּדֹרֹתָיו״, meaning: how many generations passed over Noah and he was wholehearted in all of them, meaning he stood at one steady level in his righteousness — therefore He said, 'For you I have seen righteous before Me in this generation,' for what need is there to mention that he was wholehearted also in earlier generations, since his deliverance depends on what he is there, in the generation in which he stands — and what has passed has passed. And according to what was written above, that the epithet 'wholehearted' is with reference to sexual immorality, and 'righteous' — that he did not rob, but rather would justify others from his own and give, and their sentence was sealed only on account of robbery; therefore He said, 'For you I have seen righteous' — therefore you are not included in this sealing. And He mentioned 'righteous before Me,' for the generation of the flood robbed less than the value of a perutah and were vindicated before the earthly judges, yet nevertheless they did not emerge clean in the courts of Heaven. But you are righteous also before Me, for you did not take from that which belongs to others even less than the value of a perutah."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:33.108104972Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}